// MUST BE REJECTED. A negative check on agentcore.dwschema, from the Important box under "Require a
// prior approval for the same claim" in example-policies-temporal.md. AWS quotes the service's
// rejection of an output field on a tool that declares no output schema:
//
//   predicate `AgentCore::Action::"MyTarget___verify_purchase"::response` mentions field
//   `output.orderId`, which is not declared on that event (declared fields: eventPrincipal,
//   eventResource, input.orderId, requestId, sessionId)
//
// delete_claim declares one input and no output (example-policies-reference.md), so under our
// transcription of AgentCore's schema `dogwood validate` must reject this with the same shape of
// message -- the declared fields in the same order, under the same names. If it does, the event
// schema we transcribed derives what AgentCore's derives, for this case at least.

permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"InsuranceAPI___disburse_payment",
    resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:us-west-2:123456789012:gateway/insurance-gw-a1b2c3d4e5"
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h AgentCore::Action::"InsuranceAPI___delete_claim"::response{
        eventResource: resource,
        output.claimId: context.input.claimId
    }
};

//| rejects mentions field `output.claimId`, which is not declared on that event (declared fields: eventPrincipal, eventResource, input.claimId, requestId, sessionId)
